Vectorwake, a Subspace-like MMO: settled its identity, controls and admin console, built the site and logo, hardened the client, and moved the fleet to Dallas.                                                                                                                                
Chris's rethink turned vectorwake into the match game: 3-min 4v4 melee with kits instead of greens, on a hardened fleet, and then the whole front end built to its mocks and played into shape.                                                                                                
Aug 2026: audits fixed determinism, prediction and the wire, walls went plain, the Ladder took 8x1024. Then the client was rebuilt around the match through decisions 61-73: the landing watches from the stands, and mines, standings and Discord all left the game.                          
